# =============================================================================
# Convex self-hosted fragment (issue #264) — copy to .env and adjust if needed.
# Sane defaults work out of the box for a single-machine `docker compose up`.
# =============================================================================

# Ports exposed on the host.
CONVEX_PORT=3210
CONVEX_SITE_PROXY_PORT=3211
CONVEX_DASHBOARD_PORT=6791

# URLs as reached by clients (dashboard, CLI) from outside the compose
# network. Override these if running behind a reverse proxy / real domain.
CONVEX_CLOUD_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3210
CONVEX_SITE_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3211

# OpenGroow's own required Convex function env vars (apps/convex/env.ts),
# read by the convex-bootstrap service before `npx convex deploy`. The
# unified compose stack (#266) sets these for real (dashboard URL, broker
# HMAC secrets from #265); left unset here, convex-bootstrap falls back to
# placeholders that let this fragment's schema/functions push succeed on its
# own, but are NOT meant to secure a real deployment.
# DASHBOARD_URL=http://localhost:3912
# BROKER_URL=http://broker:4300
# BROKER_KEY_ID=
# BROKER_SECRET=
# OpenClaw Control API (issue #303): in self-host, points at
# apps/openclaw-local-control (issue #305), a native host process — not a
# compose service (issue #303's Implementation Decisions: no docker.sock
# mount, so it shells out to `docker compose` directly on the host). Start it
# yourself (`pnpm --filter @opengroow/openclaw-local-control start`) before
# creating a second self-host Project. The unified stack's top-level
# docker-compose.yml overrides OPENCLAW_CONTROL_URL to
# http://host.docker.internal:4610 by default (correct for reaching the
# host from convex-backend's container); left unset here, standalone,
# apps/convex/env.ts has no default and requires it explicitly — set it to
# http://localhost:4610 for a bare `pnpm convex:dev` where both processes
# run on the host directly. Key id/secret default to "convex"/
# "convex-secret" in openclaw-local-control's own defaults — match them
# here unless you changed OPENCLAW_LOCAL_CONTROL_PORT/KEYS on that side.
# OPENCLAW_CONTROL_URL=http://host.docker.internal:4610
# OPENCLAW_CONTROL_KEY_ID=
# OPENCLAW_CONTROL_SECRET=
